# Salmon with Lemon Garlic Butter Sauce

Based on [https://cafedelites.com/crispy-seared-lemon-garlic-herb-salmon/…](https://cafedelites.com/crispy-seared-lemon-garlic-herb-salmon/#recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251209065739/https://cafedelites.com/crispy-seared-lemon-garlic-herb-salmon/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 600g [skinless salmon filets]{ ing="skinless-salmon-filets" }
- [ ] 1g [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1g [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }
- [ ] 60 ml [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, divided
- [ ] 20 ml [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 30 g [butter]{ ing="butter" }
- [ ] 8 cloves [garlic finely chopped]{ ing="garlic-finely-chopped" } or minced
- [ ] 8g [Italian parsley fresh]{ ing="italian-parsley-fresh" }, chopped, divided
- [ ] 1/2 [lemon sliced]{ ing="lemon-sliced" }

## Recipe

1. Season with [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [pepper]{ ing="pepper" }, and 1-2 tsp of [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }. Slice lengthwise into 2” strips
1. Prepare pan sauce and set aside
1. Heat the olive in a large pan over medium-high heat until hot
1. Place [salmon filets]{ ing="skinless-salmon-filets" } flesh side down and sear for 3-4 min. Then flip and sear the skin side for 2 min
1. Add in the [butter]{ ing="butter" }, garlic, 3 Tbsp of parsley, remaining [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }, and lemon slices. Stir the butter and garlic around each [filet]{ ing="skinless-salmon-filets" }

   1. Cook the salmon for a further 1-2 min or until done
1. Garnish with the remaining parsley and serve by drizzling the [butter]{ ing="butter" } over each [filet]{ ing="skinless-salmon-filets" }
